  "notes": "PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: prompt asks for flow logs for both VPCs, but both ground-truth flow logs have ResourceId on the egress VPC, so only the count (min 2) is checked, not which VPC each covers. Parameter-driven resources (ELB SLR, flow logs, KMS, log groups, roles) are off by default so they are checked as declared. Subnets are tied to the egress VPC by CIDR range, since a selector can't filter on a reference and the stated default fixes the range. A single propagation resource satisfies both tgw_route_rosa and tgw_route_egress, kept as a rare form. The ELB service-linked role may also be created by a gated custom-resource Lambda that calls CreateServiceLinkedRole for elasticloadbalancing. \"Private ROSA VPC\" is not checked directly: a negated ref (no internet gateway attached to it) can't be expressed, and a none_eq on the ROSA subnets' MapPublicIpOnLaunch can't pass the mutation control because the ground truth leaves it unset. The ROSA default route via the Transit Gateway (rosa_route_to_tgw) is the observable part. Real-output review (2026-11-10): GLM53F has no 0.0.0.0/0 route in the Transit Gateway route table, so ROSA traffic can't reach the NAT; tgw_default_route_present kept."
